# Citation metadata for Map Sheet Mosaic. Renders as "Cite this repository"
# in the GitHub sidebar. Add a DOI under `identifiers:` once a release is
# archived (e.g. on Zenodo).

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Map Sheet Mosaic in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Map Sheet Mosaic: collar removal and map-level mosaicking of scanned map sheets for ArcGIS Pro"
abstract: >
  Map Sheet Mosaic is an ArcGIS Pro Python toolbox for archives of scanned,
  georeferenced map sheets. Tool 1 identifies the sheet covered by each
  raster from its georeferencing (largest area of overlap with the sheet
  polygons of a cartogram), clips the collar with the sheet polygon while
  preserving the source cell grid, and renames the result by sheet code,
  reporting coverage, duplicate scans and pixels coinciding with the NoData
  value. Tool 2 projects an operator-selected copy of each sheet once, with
  an explicit datum transformation, onto a grid aligned to multiples of the
  cell size, and mosaics the projected sheets, grouped by any cartogram
  attribute, without further resampling.
  Every run writes a timestamped CSV report and a fixed-width log.
type: software
version: "0.1.1"
date-released: "2026-11-05"
license: Apache-2.0
